SEL: pushes now follow the relay's settings procedure: PEAT checks the model against the scanned device and the relay's ``CFG.TXT``, refuses files that aren't on the relay (unless ``sel.push_unlisted_files`` is set), uploads one file at a time with the port settings last, reads ``ERR.TXT`` after each file and stops if the relay rejects one, waits up to two minutes after Port 1 or Logic changes on SEL-700 series relays, and never writes ``SET_ALL.TXT``, ``CFG.TXT``, or ``ERR.TXT``. The status of the push and of each file, and the reason a push failed, are in the device's ``extra.push``.
